docs: state that the skills belong to their authors, not to this plugin

The panel lists and installs other people's work, and the README said nothing
about that: a reader could reasonably have taken the plugin for the origin of the
skills it shows. Both READMEs now say so up front, and carry a full
acknowledgements section modelled on the sibling Skills Hub plugin, which solves
the same problem for the same catalogue.

The statements are written against what this plugin actually does, not against a
template. Verified before writing: the npm `files` whitelist ships only lib,
locale, the icon, the patch and the READMEs, so no skill content is ever
published; the Host fetches skills from api.skillhub.cn at install time, so
nothing is hosted, mirrored or resold; and the data held is index metadata plus
the text of a single file fetched on request for the preview.

Adds NOTICE, which Apache-2.0 section 4(d) asks a distributor to carry, and names
it in `files` so it actually reaches the tarball. It records the same position in
the form that travels with the package rather than only with the repository.

Also records the licence boundary explicitly: Apache-2.0 covers this plugin's
code and never any skill, since each skill is governed by whatever its own
SKILL.md declares.
